     "body": "<p>Testing the following setup on OS X 13.0.1</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>$ java --version\njava 17.0.5 2022-10-18 LTS\nJava(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build 17.0.5+9-LTS-191)\nJava HotSpot(TM) 64-Bit Server VM (build 17.0.5+9-LTS-191, mixed mode, sharing)</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>$ bin/startup.sh\nUsing CATALINA_BASE:   /Users/dof/Development/Source/apache-tomcat-9.0.70\nUsing CATALINA_HOME:   /Users/dof/Development/Source/apache-tomcat-9.0.70\nUsing CATALINA_TMPDIR: /Users/dof/Development/Source/apache-tomcat-9.0.70/temp\nUsing JRE_HOME:        /Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/jdk-17.0.5.jdk/Contents/Home\nUsing CLASSPATH:       /Users/dof/Development/Source/apache-tomcat-9.0.70/bin/bootstrap.jar:/Users/dof/Development/Source/apache-tomcat-9.0.70/bin/tomcat-juli.jar\nUsing CATALINA_OPTS:\nTomcat started.</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>war file deploys successfully with only a single exception which I beleive is unrelated here. This appears to relate to Tomcats bootstrap attempting to restore session data from a persistant store which does not exist. Red Herring as far as we are concerned I think.</p>\n\n<p>Browsing the webapp, I can crfeate resources, view version history and delete containers. I can search successfully ffrom the search page. I used the sample tomcat-users from the documentation without any modification. </p>\n\n<p>Adding Java 17 to the CI testing matrix as per <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3867\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3867</a> will allow for deeper testing</p>",
     "created": "06/Jan/23 12:02 PM",
